                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1050: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-17T14:00:00-06:00">December 17, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. The plenary sessions of the Mediation Commission adjourned at noon today.
                    Recess of Commission begins December 18 with agreement to reconvene on or about
                    February 15, the place being left in abeyance, but with the permanent
                    secretariat remaining in San José.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
